cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "UCall: Low-Latency Client-Server Networking Stack Built around Noise Encryption, io_uring and SIMD"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/unum-cloud/UCall
url: https://github.com/unum-cloud/UCall
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.7951496
abstract: >-
  UCall is a low-latency client-server communication engine built around Noise, io_uring and
  SIMD. Application handlers stay synchronous while caller-owned polling drives
  connection state machines that overlap network I/O and retain request batches, with HTTP and Noise
  clients and servers on capability-specialized I/O backends, exposed through a C ABI with C++,
  Python, and Rust bindings.
keywords:
  - client-server communication
  - network protocol
  - noise protocol
  - io_uring
  - simd
  - http

authors:
  - family-names: Vardanian
    given-names: Ash
    alias: ashvardanian
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4882-1815
